{:edb/db-before-t 1457 :edb/db-after-t 1458 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534770 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:25:10.113Z" 13194139534770 true] [17592186096586 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309013 13194139534770 true] [17592186096586 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309027 13194139534770 true] [17592186096586 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309055 13194139534770 true] [17592186096587 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309041 13194139534770 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309035 13194139534770 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309038 13194139534770 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309048 13194139534770 true] [17592186096588 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309076 13194139534770 true] [17592186096589 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309020 13194139534770 true] [17592186096589 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309030 13194139534770 true] [17592186096589 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309062 13194139534770 true] [17592186096589 1020 #edb/ref 17592186309069 13194139534770 true] [17592186097193 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534770 true] [17592186097193 1100 "Evaluate\n\n$∫_{π}^{2π}(2\\cos^{2} 2x - x^{2})dx$." 13194139534770 false] [17592186097193 1100 "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡2x-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186097193 1145 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡2x=2[\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1)]=\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(2{cos}^{2}⁡2x-{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+x-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi +2\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2{\\pi }^{3}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4\\pi +\\pi -\\frac{1}{3}{\\pi }^{3}] \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{8{\\pi }^{3}}{3}-\\pi +\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{7{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi -7{\\pi }^{3}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi (3-7{\\pi }^{2})}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186097234 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534770 true] [17592186097234 1100 "Calculate $\\int {sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186097234 1100 "Calculate $∫\\sin^{2} xdx$." 13194139534770 false] [17592186097234 1145 "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186288705 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/5e40f35729a8e3df9f8403cad85bf0c4e6045733616c86cc399548a901c03ac7.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534770 true] [17592186288705 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008673/assets/5e40f35729a8e3df9f8403cad85bf0c4e6045733616c86cc399548a901c03ac7.png)\n\nA region in the $xy$-plane is bounded by the curve $y=2{cos}^{2}⁡x+x-1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2},$ as shown above. The area of the region is\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534770 false] [17592186288706 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309034 13194139534770 true] [17592186303641 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534770 true] [17592186303641 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039635/assets/41304b7f8cbaf3df778e0f079a1651d2846f94dc74012db3b2ce936144eac8c7.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534770 false] [17592186309013 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309014 13194139534770 true] [17592186309013 1089 "q-114677" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309013 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534770 true] [17592186309013 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309013 1113 #uuid "3ab694ca-3522-5886-8748-89bccc4c5cb5" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309013 1145 "In this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,⇒\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]+C \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309015 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309016 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309017 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309018 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309019 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1041 "selection" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309016 13194139534770 true] [17592186309014 1110 #uuid "fe5ffd91-0b39-50fc-acdc-6bc6d557bb50" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309015 1034 "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309015 1111 #uuid "fcfc0fe7-b049-5e5c-a53b-a59ca96f87f7" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309016 1034 "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309016 1111 #uuid "ac2b56b2-ccad-5fdb-aabb-5b793ad9876d" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309017 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309017 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309017 1111 #uuid "66f3655c-8a66-5167-889e-e00142c53e26" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309018 1034 "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309018 1111 #uuid "eed7b905-9473-586f-98d4-3affc767e218" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309019 1034 "-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309019 1111 #uuid "f40b31fb-8e5f-5415-b935-ae2cb4f42e00" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309020 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309021 13194139534770 true] [17592186309020 1089 "q-114685" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309020 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534770 true] [17592186309020 1100 "$\\int (3{x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309020 1113 #uuid "582936cd-ad73-5d84-91d0-0e021f4969e3" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309020 1145 "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{x}^{2}-{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309022 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309023 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309024 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309025 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309026 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1041 "selection" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309026 13194139534770 true] [17592186309021 1110 #uuid "a96ac087-cb16-5505-9f0e-bc7da79090a8" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309022 1034 "{x}^{2}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309022 1111 #uuid "c72a8e57-4613-5191-8274-f501ea22b3fb" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309023 1034 "3{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309023 1111 #uuid "d4fea5ab-00dd-5c8f-af2b-5a9fa64be6e9" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309024 1034 "3{x}^{2}-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309024 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309024 1111 #uuid "d24213e3-f693-5cdd-a3b9-9605a3c24a0c" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309025 1034 "{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309025 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309025 1111 #uuid "4cb5bb08-f535-5922-8a75-2488d0ede329" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309026 1034 "{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+C" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309026 1111 #uuid "7b3d1c61-6a2d-50ce-aad5-a6ce6f1a5483" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309027 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309028 13194139534770 true] [17592186309027 1089 "q-348705" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309027 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534770 true] [17592186309027 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040629/assets/ae150f223d210225b6490bebb859909b07842a8b7abb41137cf0206312aead2e.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}),$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=0$ and $x=\\pi ,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309027 1113 #uuid "a1ec3a42-2a31-535c-b647-69694b17ef74" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309027 1145 "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309028 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309029 13194139534770 true] [17592186309028 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534770 true] [17592186309028 1041 "field-1" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309028 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309029 13194139534770 true] [17592186309028 1110 #uuid "921109d2-472c-5ad6-83e6-9ed2084f48fb" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309029 1034 "5" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309029 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309029 1111 #uuid "d8d6c8a7-d0d6-5252-8063-4cdeae52ff73" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309030 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309031 13194139534770 true] [17592186309030 1089 "q-348724" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309030 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534770 true] [17592186309030 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309030 1113 #uuid "3ea82d24-c80c-5089-8bd5-efac42e51f83" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309030 1145 "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309031 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309032 13194139534770 true] [17592186309031 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309033 13194139534770 true] [17592186309031 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534770 true] [17592186309031 1041 "field-1" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309031 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309032 13194139534770 true] [17592186309031 1110 #uuid "98143ef5-3ba7-5bf3-8e38-a70e9df4babe" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309032 1034 "\\frac{2\\pi^2}{3}" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309032 1111 #uuid "db6c166e-72c3-552d-b524-d11113f0a364" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309033 1034 "\\frac{\\pi^2}{3}" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309033 1111 #uuid "76d59c68-af09-5e9e-a3c5-93ed10ab20f8" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309034 1034 "2\\pi^2" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534770 true] [17592186309034 1111 #uuid "8d1c4de3-983f-562f-a2f4-b741d4cd634a" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309035 1017 #edb/ref 17592186309036 13194139534770 true] [17592186309035 1089 "q-348837" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309035 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534770 true] [17592186309035 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309035 1113 #uuid "6549d8b4-dd98-5be4-8fa6-e23e672f25d6" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309035 1145 "Recall  ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ so letting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}) & =1-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2})-2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}) \\\\  & =1-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta )={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{3x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))={sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}(1-3{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{3x}{2}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}(1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3}(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{1}{2}x)\\,|}_{\\pi /3}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi }{3}]-[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}] \\\\  & =[0-\\frac{\\pi }{3}]-[0-\\frac{\\pi }{6}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309036 1000 #edb/ref 17592186309037 13194139534770 true] [17592186309036 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534770 true] [17592186309036 1041 "field-1" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309036 1104 #edb/ref 17592186309037 13194139534770 true] [17592186309036 1110 #uuid "f468b95c-c083-5e7f-aa17-9c9e4cce81d7" 13194139534770 true] [17592186309037 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi}{6}" 13